EE 460N Lab 2 -- expected output for lab2test.asm
Name 1: Alan Schwartz          UTEID 1: as237333
Name 2: Siddhartha Guntupalli  UTEID 2: sg59532

How to reproduce
----------------
  gcc -std=c99 -o simulate lc3bsim2.c
  assemble lab2test.asm isaprogram
  ./simulate isaprogram

  LC-3b-SIM> go
  LC-3b-SIM> mdump 0x309e 0x30cc
  LC-3b-SIM> rdump
  LC-3b-SIM> quit

The program is assembled at x3000. DATA lands at x309a, RES at x309e and
RESEND at x30ce. Every test writes its result into RES, so one mdump of
x309e..x30cc covers the whole run.


Expected memory, x309e..x30cc
-----------------------------
  addr      value    what it checks
  0x309e :  0x1239   ADD imm5 form, x1234 + 5
  0x30a0 :  0xbe01   ADD SR2 form, x1234 + xABCD, carry out of bit 15 dropped
  0x30a2 :  0x1234   AND imm5 form, imm5 #-2 sign-extends to xFFFE
  0x30a4 :  0x0204   AND SR2 form, x1234 & xABCD
  0x30a6 :  0x123b   XOR imm5 form, x1234 ^ x000F
  0x30a8 :  0xb9f9   XOR SR2 form, x1234 ^ xABCD
  0x30aa :  0xedcb   NOT, assembled as XOR with imm5 x1F
  0x30ac :  0x2340   LSHF x1234 by 4, bits shifted past bit 15 dropped
  0x30ae :  0x0abc   RSHFL xABCD by 4, zero fill
  0x30b0 :  0xfabc   RSHFA xABCD by 4, sign fill (xABCD is negative)
  0x30b2 :  0xffcd   LDB of the low byte of xABCD, sign extended
  0x30b4 :  0xffab   LDB of the high byte of xABCD, sign extended
  0x30b6 :  0x0003   BR taken on z, not taken on n, then unconditional
  0x30b8 :  0x000f   backward BRp loop, 5+4+3+2+1
  0x30ba :  0x1234   STW with a negative offset6 (RESEND-20)
  0x30bc :  0x0034   STB wrote only the low byte, high byte still zero
  0x30be :  0x1234   LDW with a negative offset6 (RESEND-52 = DATA)
  0x30c0 :  0x0007   LEA did not disturb the condition codes
  0x30c2 :  0x000a   JSR with PCoffset11, then RET
  0x30c4 :  0x3082   return address JSR stored in R7 (incremented PC)
  0x30c6 :  0x000b   JSRR with BaseR, then RET
  0x30c8 :  0x0001   JMP skipped over the instruction after it
  0x30ca :  0x0000   unused
  0x30cc :  0x0000   unused


Expected final state (rdump after go)
-------------------------------------
  Instruction Count : 84
  PC                : 0x0000
  CCs: N = 0  Z = 0  P = 1
  Registers:
  0: 0x309a     &DATA, left by LEA
  1: 0x1234
  2: 0xabcd
  3: 0x309e     &RES, left by LEA
  4: 0x3094     &SUB2, the JSRR target
  5: 0x0001
  6: 0x000b     set by SUB2
  7: 0x308e     incremented PC saved by the HALT trap

PC is 0x0000 because TRAP x25 reads the trap vector table, which the shell
zeroes out, and the shell halts the simulator when PC becomes 0. R7 holding
0x308e confirms TRAP saved the incremented PC before jumping.
